Package: switchfix
Version: 0.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6, libdbus-1-3
Recommends: policykit-1
Maintainer: SwitchFix contributors <switchfix@localhost>
Homepage: https://github.com/switchfix/switchfix
Description: Fix text typed in the wrong keyboard layout (EN↔RU)
 SwitchFix is a KDE Plasma tray utility in the spirit of Punto Switcher /
 Keyboop. It converts text typed in the wrong keyboard layout, switches the
 system layout, and (in later phases) will add spelling fixes and snippet
 expansion.
 .
 Features (MVP):
  * Convert selection (Ctrl+F1) via clipboard-marker protocol
  * Convert last word (Ctrl+F2) via in-memory keystroke buffer
  * Terminal mode (Ctrl+Shift+F1)
  * Toggle on/off (Ctrl+Pause) and tray menu
  * System layout switch through org.kde.KeyboardLayouts
 .
 Privacy: no network, no keylogging persistence. The keystroke buffer is
 RAM-only and optional. Membership in group 'input' is required for global
 hotkeys and uinput injection.
